Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Page: publish runtime flag, log stage RSS, and preserve
 partial results on later failure

- export_runtime_env() at import so children and the vendored MEME wrapper make
  the same shared-cloud decision as Python.
- Persist the mutable result object to session_state up-front and mutate in place,
  so a failure in motif QC / ordering / packaging never discards completed
  phylogeny, gene-structure, CDD or MEME results.
- Guard the previously-unwrapped tail (motif_qc, choose_order, package) and the
  final download button; a failed reproducibility package now shows a clear notice
  while the computed tables/tree/alignment remain available.
- log_event() markers (run.start, run.analysis_done) record RSS at stage
  boundaries for Cloud-log diagnosis.
- Update est2genome fast-path tests to patch the sandbox runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXzHvNkP6ybDucH19uqYv2
